xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">Located inside the Foundational Space, the double entity known as the &#8220;Shadow Dance&#8221; consists of two humanoid silhouette-shaped figures, one appearing to be\ of the male gender, and other of the female gender. Although not having any facial features, their outlines indicate they wear what appear to be fancy suits, with patterns and details that resemble 40s period type clothing. No explanation can be found fo\r these patterns, and their movement coordination simulate varied styles of dances for all their actions, especially attacking. The energy they&#8217;re appear to be made of is of similar composition of an Ontological Source&#8217;s, possibly linking thei\r origin to those beings, although this energy is coupled with a bigger energy pattern, which currently shows signs of corruption, and the nature of it is unknown \(It is not clear if this corruption is a natural byproduct of the entity or if it was cause\d by external influence\). As they are yet to be discovered in a provable manner, there is no known information about visible weaknesses or strategies for subjugation except for intuitively attempting to align one&#8217;s movements with the &#8220;dance&#\8221; to match it.</span></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 76.864 571.302 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj66 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Dif)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240915124553-03'00')/NM(1136aaeffc294a48afa27816b1ee9af3)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Ac