 \(Dif/3\). His exclusive movements are the\ &quot;Hot Moves&quot;, which grant him 5 Drive for each successful realization.</span></p></body>)/Rect[181.528 655.802 516.439 711.812]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj71 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Female Dancer - The apparently male silhouette disposes of dance movements to realize any actions, and when working together with the male one, both can cause double trouble!\(Damage = x2\) To attack, she uses Offensive Moves. To defend or evade, Defensiv\e Moves. In case she loses her rhythm, she can recover her Pacing to match the music again and recover lost CS \(Dif/3\). Her exclusive movements are the "Smooth Moves", which create 3 afterimages of her \(and 3 of the male one if he is still on the field\\), with 1 CS each, and for each that is damaged, 1 of enemy Drive is converted into Antimatter.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 8.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240919172429-03'00')/NM(e5d6d6beb785412c93a0ea2c110921d7)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Helvetica;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr">Female Dancer - The apparently male silhouette disposes of dance movements to realize any actions, and when working together with the male one, both can cause double trouble!\(Damage = x2\) To attac\k, she uses Offensive Moves. To defend or evade, Defensive Moves. In case she loses her rhythm, she can recover her Pacing to match the music again and recover lost CS \(Dif/3\). Her exclusive movements are the &quot;Smooth Moves&quot;, which create 3 aft\erimages of her \(and 3 of the male one if he is still on the field\), with 1 CS each, and for each that is damaged, 1 of enemy Drive is converted into Antimatter.</p></body>)/Rect[182.837 557.74 518.402 628.55]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj72 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(                                                                                                         Notes\r)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 17.1 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 17.1pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240919171612-03'00')/NM(5f15e8eb9fc54a00959a0547e7205bd6)/Page 3/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:17.1pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">                                                                                                         Notes&#13;</span></p></body>)/Rect[270.634 669.124 325.311 727.274]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj73 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240915124026-03'00')/NM(d22bedd642ee4046b0d883ddb2b6cb22)/Page 3/Rect[67.0267 634.469 261.76 646.669]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj74 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj75 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj76 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj77 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj78 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj79 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj80 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj81 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj82 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj83 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj84 0 obj<</W 0.0>>endobj85 0 obj<</W 14.0>>endobjtrailer
